# AI PAN Detection & Masking Protocol

## Objective
Detect and timestamp both full PANs (12-19 digits) and partial PAN segments (4/6/8 digits) in audio transcripts using fuzzy Luhn validation with contextual awareness.

## Input Requirements
- Context: ${Explain}
- Confirmed PANs: ${ListPAN}
- Transcript: 
${SegmentsAndWords}

## Processing Pipeline

1. **Initial Scan**
   - Extract all 4+ digit sequences
   - Normalize (remove spaces/hyphens)
   - Categorize by length:
     - 12-19 digits: Full PAN candidates
     - 4/6/8 digits: Partial PAN candidates

2. **Context Validation**
   For partial PANs require either:
   - Preceding trigger phrase ("last 4 digits", "CVV", etc.)
   - Subsequent full PAN reference
   - Payment-related conversation context

3. **Luhn Verification**
   - Full PANs must pass Luhn check
   - Partial PANs must match substring of confirmed PANs

4. **Fuzzy Matching**
   - Allow max 2 character edits
   - Cross-check against confirmed PAN list
   - Calculate confidence score (100% for exact matches)

## Output Specification
<contiguous_sequences>
  <!-- Full PAN with high confidence -->
  [start_timestamp] --> [end_timestamp]: [FULL] 4111-1111-1111-1111 (confidence: 98%)
  
  <!-- Valid partial PAN -->
  [start_timestamp] --> [end_timestamp]: [PARTIAL] "verify 1111" (linked: 4111...1111)
  
  <!-- Rejected match -->
  [start_timestamp] --> [end_timestamp]: [IGNORED] "room 4111" (reason: no PAN context)
</contiguous_sequences>

## Confidence Thresholds
- 100%: Exact match to known PAN
- 95-99%: Luhn valid + 1 edit difference
- 90-94%: Partial match with strong context
- <90%: Automatically rejected

## Temporal Rules
- Maximum duration:
  - Full PAN: 60 seconds
  - Partial PAN: 30 seconds
- Timestamp alignment:
  - 15-second sliding window
  - Merge overlapping segments

## Special Cases
- AMEX 15-digit cards
- Spaces/hyphens in PANs
- Multi-speaker PAN fragments
- Background noise disruptions